### What steps can reproduce the bug?

When using the hono/jwk middleware  with a jwks_uri pointing to the Microsoft Entra ID JWKS endpoint, verifying a valid JWT signed with RS256 fails with the following error:
```
DOMException [DataError]: Invalid JWK "kty" Parameter
    at Object.hmacImportKey (node:internal/crypto/mac:140:15)
    at SubtleCrypto.importKey (node:internal/crypto/webcrypto:588:10)
    at importPublicKey (file:///.../node_modules/hono/dist/utils/jwt/jws.js:58:32)
    at verifying (file:///.../node_modules/hono/dist/utils/jwt/jws.js:13:27)
    at verify (file:///.../node_modules/hono/dist/utils/jwt/jwt.js:59:26)
    at Object.verifyFromJwks (file:///.../node_modules/hono/dist/utils/jwt/jwt.js:103:16)
```

The issue appears to be in the `verifyFromJwks` function within ```node_modules/hono/dist/utils/jwt/jwt.js```
It fetches the JWKS and finds the correct key (matchingKey) using the kid.
The Microsoft Entra ID JWKS keys do not include an explicit alg property within the key object itself:
[Entra ID common JWKS endpoint](https://login.microsoftonline.com/common/discovery/v2.0/keys)

The function then calls the internal verify function using the algorithm from the key: ```await verify(token, matchingKey, matchingKey.alg);```
Since matchingKey.alg is undefined, the verify function ```(verify = async (token, publicKey, alg = "HS256") => ...) ``` incorrectly defaults to using the "HS256" algorithm.
Attempting to import/use the fetched RSA public key with HMAC parameters (HS256) triggers the ```DOMException [DataError]: Invalid JWK "kty" Parameter``` from the underlying crypto library.

Repro code:
```
import { serve } from '@hono/node-server';
import { Hono } from 'hono';
import { jwk } from 'hono/jwk';
import { jwt } from 'hono/jwt';

const app = new Hono();

app.use(
  '/auth/*',
  jwk({
    jwks_uri: 'https://login.microsoftonline.com/common/discovery/v2.0/keys',
  })
);

app.onError((err, c) => {
  console.error(err);
  return c.json({ error: 'Internal Server Error', message: err }, 500);
});

app.get('/auth/page', (c) => {
  const payload = c.get('jwtPayload');
  return c.json(payload);
});
serve({
  fetch: app.fetch,
  port: 3000
}, (info) => {
  console.log(`Server is running on http://localhost:${info.port}`);
});
```
I tested the following change below in the function `verifyFromJwks`, which fixed the issue, although I'm not sure if this would break any other functionality

from:
`  return await verify(token, matchingKey, matchingKey.alg);`
to:
`return await verify(token, matchingKey, header.alg);`

### What is the expected behavior?

To return the jwt payload

### What do you see instead?

```
DOMException [DataError]: Invalid JWK "kty" Parameter
    at Object.hmacImportKey (node:internal/crypto/mac:140:15)
    at SubtleCrypto.importKey (node:internal/crypto/webcrypto:588:10)
    at importPublicKey (file:///.../node_modules/hono/dist/utils/jwt/jws.js:58:32)
    at verifying (file:///.../node_modules/hono/dist/utils/jwt/jws.js:13:27)
    at verify (file:///.../node_modules/hono/dist/utils/jwt/jwt.js:59:26)
    at Object.verifyFromJwks (file:///.../node_modules/hono/dist/utils/jwt/jwt.js:103:16)
```

